{"id": "EUVD-2026-96891", "enisaUuid": "0d9940a2-8f50-3f7b-a4b5-ade11950bda0", "description": "Cheshire Cat AI core through 2.0.23 contains a stored cross-site scripting vulnerability in the uploads plugin that allows authenticated users to upload HTML files via POST /uploads without type restrictions. Attackers can send the public GET /uploads/{path} URL to a signed-in victim, executing script in the application origin with the victim's access_token cookie, including administrators.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T12:19:34", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T13:18:28", "baseScore": 5.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:P/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind03/cheshire-cat-uploads-stored-html-same-origin-xss", "https://github.com/cheshire-cat-ai/core/blob/c22731e7009ac89835b1d7b1cabc5989d998ec3e/src/cat/scaffold/plugins/uploads/endpoints.py#L28-L96", "https://github.com/cheshire-cat-ai/core", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/cheshire-cat-ai-core-through-2.0.23-stored-xss-via-uploads-plugin"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108725", "GHSA-37wv-8fg5-p97x"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1b94ffb5-681d-3976-bb2a-e50cb8b4f25e", "product": {"name": "core", "vendor": {"name": "OPNsense"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.0.23"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b4b876b3-308b-3a17-8fc2-4ae28ab9ee1e", "vendor": {"name": "cheshire-cat-ai"}}], "isExploited": false}